From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:32:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Name the low-power
 microphone's DART stream

T8132's AOP audio node falls back to apple,t6041-aop-audio, whose driver
captures the low-power microphone into a host ring on the node's DART
stream, and only where the node names that stream.

The J604's ADT (26B123) describes the low-power microphone as T6041's
does: iop-audio-controller/lp-mic-device (identifier iapl) and
lp-mic-io-buffer-device (identifier xpda, io-buffer-size 0xbb800), whose
iommu-parent is dart-aop/mapper-admac-base-ns at reg 8, as on the J614s.
Name aop_dart stream 8 on the J604's audio node, the stream admac1
already uses.

Other T8132 Macs are not checked, so the stream stays out of t8132.dtsi.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
index b312234a00..41436dd258 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
@@ -105,6 +105,11 @@ &sound_jack {
 &aop_audio {
 	apple,chassis-name = "J604";
 	apple,machine-kind = "MacBook Pro";
+	/*
+	 * The low-power microphone ring: the stream of the ADT's
+	 * lp-mic-io-buffer-device (mapper-admac-base-ns), shared with admac1.
+	 */
+	iommus = <&aop_dart 8>;
 };
 
